{:edb/db-before-t 12352 :edb/db-after-t 12353 :edb/tx-data [[13194139545665 50 #inst "2026-11-03T08:00:24.964Z" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748212 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748221 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748224 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748234 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748246 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748247 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748249 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748280 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748285 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748303 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748306 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748320 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748326 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748341 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1038 #edb/ref 17592186748343 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186166788 1040 #edb/ref 17592186694214 13194139545665 17592186576411 false] [17592186166788 1040 #edb/ref 17592186748370 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186693815 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186693821 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186693830 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694166 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694194 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694197 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694208 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694216 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694227 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694244 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694256 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694258 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694284 1173 true 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694294 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{dy}{dt}= \\\\ \\left(y - 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} \\\\ + e^{-2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186694294 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} + \\left(y + 1\\right) = \\left(y + 1\\right) + \\left(\\left(y - 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}\\right).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." 13194139545665 17592186576411 false] [17592186694294 1074 "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nThe original equation requires $y - 1>0$.\n\nIsolating the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = y^{2} \\ln{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} - 2 y \\ln{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}.\n$$\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=2$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c - 1 \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ L(c) &= c + 1 \\\\  &= 3 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(c + 1\\right) + \\left(\\left(c - 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(c - 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}\\right) \\\\  &= e^{-2} + 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=1 + e$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c - 1 \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e \\right)} \\\\  &= 1 \\\\ L(c) &= c + 1 \\\\  &= 2 + e \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(c + 1\\right) + \\left(\\left(c - 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(c - 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}\\right) \\\\  &= e^{-2} + 2 + e + e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=e^{-1} + 1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c - 1 \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)} \\\\  &= -1 \\\\ L(c) &= c + 1 \\\\  &= e^{-1} + 2 \\\\ R(c) &= \\left(c + 1\\right) + \\left(\\left(c - 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(c - 1 \\right)} + e^{-2}\\right) \\\\  &= e^{-1} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=e^{-1} + 1$." 13194139545665 17592186576411 false] [17592186694294 1074 "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $y - 1>0$.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(c)= \\\\ \\left(c - 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(c - 1 \\right)} \\\\ + e^{-2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\n- For $c=1 + e$: Use $\\ln{\\left(e \\right)}=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(1 + e)= \\\\ e^{-2} + e^{2} \\ln{\\left(e \\right)} \\\\ =e^{-2} + e^{2}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=2$: Use $\\ln{\\left(1 \\right)}=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=1 \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} + e^{-2} \\\\ &=e^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=e^{-1} + 1$: Use $\\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)}=-1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(e^{-1} + 1)= \\\\ \\frac{\\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)}}{e^{2}} + e^{-2} \\\\ =0\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=e^{-1} + 1$." 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748205 1080 "true" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748205 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [1759218674