\\ \\left(y + 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(y + 1 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748212 1072 #uuid "141a55c9-d09e-52ce-941e-f884a7716745" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748212 1074 "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $y + 1>0$.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(c)= \\\\ \\left(c + 1\\right)^{2} \\ln{\\left(c + 1 \\right)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\n- For $c=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=4 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-1 + e$: Use $\\ln{\\left(e \\right)}=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1 + e) &=e^{2} \\ln{\\left(e \\right)} \\\\ &=e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=0$: Use $\\ln{\\left(1 \\right)}=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) &=1 \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=0$." 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748213 1080 "false" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748213 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748213 1083 #uuid "16124f30-0b52-55e1-8a25-43384f85d48b" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748214 1080 "true" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748214 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748214 1083 #uuid "17d46587-f1a3-5fd2-8397-52cfae64551e" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748215 1080 "true" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748215 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748215 1083 #uuid "197ca168-676a-5525-a02a-13f76c4b885f" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [17592186748216 1080 "false" 13194139545665 17592186576411 true] [1759218